course: dictionary
lesson: 8613
title: Scream and the feelings behind it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scream is a loud, high cry. People scream because of fear, pain, anger or excitement. «He did it, the glass cracked, and a toddler inside screamed.» The sound is high and loud, so the toddler is probably upset or hurt.
explain: Scream can be a verb or a noun. «The fox began to scream» uses it as a verb, the action of crying out. «Let out a scream» uses it as a noun, the sound itself. The words around it tell you which one it is.
explain: Context also shows the feeling. In a story, a scream often means fear or surprise. Children scream with fun on rides, and that is a happy scream. Read the sentence around the word to find out which feeling it is.
explain: Informally, «It was a scream» means something was very funny. Nobody was shouting. Your friend is describing a joke, not a noise.
fact: «Scream» means to cry out with a loud, high sound because of fear, pain, anger or excitement.
fact: A scream is a loud, high cry.
fact: Useful phrases are «scream for help», «let out a scream» and «scream with laughter».
fact: In safety lessons, screaming and shouting «No!» is a way to get help if you are in danger.
fact: Informally, «It was a scream» means it was very funny.
exercise: «If a strange dog runs at you, do not run or scream: be a tree.» In this advice, what should you do instead of screaming? | *Stand still, fold your arms in close and stay quiet | Shout at the dog | Climb the nearest fence | Run as fast as you can
exercise: «The scream heard on winter nights is often a fox calling to find a mate.» What is the scream usually? | *A fox calling | A bird singing at dawn | A child playing in the snow | A door slamming shut
exercise: Your friend laughs and says, «That joke was a scream!» What does she mean? | It was very cold | It was very frightening | It was very loud | *It was very funny
test: Which phrase means to call out for help when you are in danger? | *Scream and shout | Scream for help | Scream with laughter | Let out a scream of joy
test: «He did it, the glass cracked, and a toddler inside screamed.» What is the toddler doing? | Singing a song | *Crying out loudly in fear or pain | Laughing quietly | Sleeping
exam: In «The scream rang out across the playground», which word is a noun? | across | rang | *scream | out
